---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { loadCrates, crateByName } from '../artifacts/crates';
import { loadSiteCounts } from '../artifacts/counts';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import '../styles/about.css';

// Counts and download numbers come from the dated snapshots, never from the copy.
const [counts, crates] = await Promise.all([loadSiteCounts(), loadCrates()]);
const number = new Intl.NumberFormat('en-US');
const downloads = (name: string) => {
  const crate = crateByName(crates.crates, name);
  return crate ? `${number.format(crate.downloads)} downloads` : 'on crates.io';
};
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description={`Background, education, and the work I do: a WGU B.S. in AI Engineering (expected September 2027), ${counts.crates} published Rust crates, synthetic-factory, and merged upstream PRs.`}>
  <section class="page-intro" aria-labelledby="about-title">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1 id="about-title">About me.</h1>
    <p>I'm {site.fullName}. I live in San Marcos, Texas, and I'm open to relocating.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="about-profile" aria-label="Professional background">
    <figure><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="/assets/raul-cardenas-montoya-256.webp 256w, /assets/raul-cardenas-montoya-512.webp 512w" sizes="(max-width: 760px) 90vw, 380px" /><img src="/assets/raul-cardenas-montoya-512.jpg" srcset="/assets/raul-cardenas-montoya-256.jpg 256w, /assets/raul-cardenas-montoya-512.jpg 512w" sizes="(max-width: 760px) 90vw, 380px" width="512" height="512" alt="Raul Cardenas Montoya" loading="eager" /></picture><figcaption>Raul Cardenas Montoya, San Marcos, TX.</figcaption></figure>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>Most of what I build is infrastructure for agentic systems, synthetic data, and model evaluation. synthetic-factory is a synthetic-data platform where unknown provenance resolves to blocked and every record replays from its pack, seed, and actions. I've published {counts.datasets} datasets on Hugging Face as of {counts.datasetsAsOf}{counts.factoryDatasets > 0 ? `, ${counts.factoryDatasets} of them from it` : ''}. agoge-forger is a local-first LoRA/QLoRA post-training harness with immutable manifests, split-integrity checks, and leakage detection. I wrote up what running a swarm of coding agents taught me about verification in <a href="/notes/done-is-a-claim/">Done is a claim</a>.</p>
      <p>I've published {counts.crates} Rust crates on crates.io as of {counts.cratesAsOf}, including neuromod ({downloads('neuromod')}) and nir-rs ({downloads('nir-rs')}). The spiking-network demo on the homepage runs on four of them. Upstream, I implemented the xAI/Grok provider in agent-afk, and I added Linux support and Devin usage tracking to UsagePal. Both sets of PRs are merged.</p>
      <p>I'm working toward a B.S. in Artificial Intelligence Engineering at Western Governors University, expected September 2027. Before that I took coursework at Texas State University (Spring 2026), Concordia University Texas (Computer Science, Fall 2025), and Austin Community College (Business Administration, 2019–2025).</p>
      <p>I work in Rust, Python, Julia, and CUDA C/C++, mostly on Fedora Linux. The fastest way to reach me is <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>, and my <a href={site.resumePath}>résumé is a PDF</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
